From 3b1b94c7566f7603d36906ac4f5bf2a4178b3f8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mohammed <91819504+mohammed7s@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:04:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] computercontrol: recheck caller permissions and policy
 before publishing a session

Permissions and policy can change while a session is being constructed
or while its consent dialog is open. Using the caller's captured UID,
package and user, recheck before construction and again before
publication: the assistant role, the notification and Computer Control
permissions, managed-device policy and the Computer Control AppOp.

"Allow once" still applies to the targets approved by the current dialog,
but it cannot override an explicit AppOp denial. A normal agent that
loses its permission is not reclassified as a test agent.

Test: atest VirtualDeviceServicesTests:ComputerControlSessionProcessorTest
Test: atest VirtualDeviceServicesTests:ComputerControlAllowlistControllerTest

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
